summary:
- topic: FY2026 Budget Outlook
  text: The Superintendent presented a challenging FY2026 budget context, stating
    a simple rollover of current services would require an 11.4% local increase. Pressures
    include expiring federal funds, rising special education needs, and reduced philanthropic
    funding. A non-essential spending freeze is in effect, and reductions in employee
    positions are anticipated.
- topic: Athletic Complex Referendum
  text: 'Following extensive discussion, the Board voted 4-3 to recommend a November
    2025 referendum for the SPHS athletic complex. The approved motion puts two choices
    before voters: a $5.10 million project with a synthetic turf stadium field or
    a $4.29 million project with a natural grass field. Both options include a new
    track, lighting, and permanent restrooms, but exclude practice fields and a storage
    building from the original proposal.'
- topic: Pre-K Program Expansion
  text: Assistant Superintendent Dr. Prince announced a 'mixed delivery' pre-K partnership
    pilot for the 2025-26 school year. The district will partner with Chickadee Toddler
    Care and Preschool and the United Way of Southern Maine to add up to 32 new, free
    pre-K seats at no cost to the local budget, funded entirely by state pass-through
    dollars.
- topic: Policy Approvals
  text: The Board unanimously approved several policies on second reading, including
    the student code of conduct (JIC), job descriptions (GAB), school board legal
    status (BBB), and board member conflict of interest (BCB). Policy JLCE (Do Not
    Resuscitate Requests) was rescinded via the consent agenda.
- topic: 2025-2026 School Calendar
  text: The Board unanimously approved the school calendar for the 2025-2026 school
    year. It includes 175 student days and five built-in potential weather days before
    the Juneteenth holiday.
- topic: Commitment to DEI
  text: The Board Chair and Superintendent both reaffirmed the district's strong commitment
    to its Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) values in response to national political
    pressures, stating the district will continue to do what is right for all students.
- topic: Student and Staff Recognition
  text: The student representative and superintendent highlighted numerous student
    achievements, including a new state record in track and field and the success
    of the SPHS boys' and girls' basketball teams in reaching the state championships.
    The retirements of several long-serving staff members were also acknowledged.
